.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH soundcraft-cli-convert 1  "convert " 
.SH NAME
soundcraft\-cli\-convert \- Convert an audio file: resample, change the bit depth, normalize
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsoundcraft\-cli convert\fR [\fB\-\-bit\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-normalize\fR] [\fB\-\-dither\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-dither\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-place\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIIN\fR> <\fIOUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert an audio file: resample, change the bit depth, normalize
.PP
Dithers only when the output loses resolution, unless \-\-dither or \-\-no\-dither says otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bit\-depth\fR \fI<16|24|32f>\fR [default: 24]
The output\*(Aqs bit depth
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
16
.IP \(bu 2
24
.IP \(bu 2
32f
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<HZ>\fR
Resample to this sample rate
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\fR
Normalize the peak to \-0.1 dBFS
.TP
\fB\-\-dither\fR
Always dither
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-dither\fR
Never dither
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
Allow an <OUT> that is the <IN> file, replacing the original
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIIN\fR>
The audio file to read (wav, wave, bwf, rf64, aif, aiff, aifc, flac, mp3, mp2, mp1, ogg, oga, m4a, m4b, aac, mp4, adts, caf, mkv, webm)
.TP
<\fIOUT\fR>
The audio file to write; its extension picks the format (wav, wave, bwf, aif, aiff, flac)
